<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro">
  <!-- =====================================================================
       Human wearer + SRL backpack mount. VISUAL REFERENCE ONLY.

       FRAME CONVENTION (inherited, do not "fix" casually):
         x = lateral (left/right)   y = fore/aft, wearer faces +y   z = up
       This is NOT the usual ROS x-forward convention, but it is what the
       existing legs (x = +/-0.07) and backpack (y = -0.12, i.e. behind)
       already encode, and the arm mounts follow it.

       KINEMATIC CONTRACT
       Every joint <origin> in this file is unchanged from the version
       that the workspace anchor and home poses were derived against.
       All proportion work below is done with per-<visual> origins, so
       no link frame moves and the arm mounts are bit-identical. New
       links are visual leaves and enter no existing chain.

       The mounts sit ~0.18 m BELOW the wearer's shoulder line. Raising
       them to shoulder height is a mount-origin change and is therefore
       NOT done here - see the proposal in the accompanying notes.

       NO COLLISION GEOMETRY, deliberately: these links carry <visual>
       only and appear nowhere in the SRDF, so MoveIt does not know the
       wearer exists and will never plan around them. Adding <collision>
       here would silently change planning behaviour.
       ===================================================================== -->
  <!-- =================================================================
       ARM MOUNT — DERIVED, not searched. See CLAUDE.md for the full working.

       THE MODEL. One plate, so the plate NORMAL is mirror-symmetric. But the
       CLOCKING — which hole on the arm's circular base flange the bolts go
       through — is a per-arm assembly choice and is NOT mirrored. That is
       still "the arms bolt to one plate", and it is what makes the geometry
       solvable at all:

         with a fully mirror-symmetric mount,
             |right_P_HOME - mirror(left_P_HOME)| = |v_R - M v_L| = 1.3837 m
         INDEPENDENT of the rotation — the mount cancels algebraically. The
         two home posture vectors are 119.6 deg apart in their own base
         frames, and two vectors rigidly 119.6 deg apart cannot both point
         forward. A search over mirror-symmetric rotations therefore CANNOT
         succeed, which is why two of them produced arms buried in the torso.
         Allowing independent clocking drops that residual to 0.0889 m.

       THE DERIVATION, in closed form. The EE offset in the ARM BASE frame is
       fixed by the joint angles (verified against the stock Gen3 to 1e-9 m),
       so |EE - mount| = |v| is FORCED: the reachable EE set is a sphere. The
       target DIRECTION fixes two rotational DOF exactly, by shortest arc. The
       third DOF is a spin about that direction which does not move the EE at
       all — it rotates the arm's PATH — and it is chosen by the minimum
       clearance of EVERY intermediate link, which is the thing it controls.

       POSITION ALSO CHANGED, and it had to be. At the old (0.15, -0.12) the
       Gen3 base tube (r=0.046, 0.171 m long) starts 0.010 m from the torso
       box, so over EVERY possible rotation the best achievable clearance for
       base_link — a link NO joint moves — was +0.0097 m. The 0.15 m floor was
       infeasible by a factor of 15 before any rotation was chosen. Moving the
       mount onto the BACK of the pack rather than its front face fixes it.
       ================================================================= -->
  <xacro:macro name="human_backpack"
               params="parent
                       mount_x:=0.20 mount_y:=-0.20 mount_z:=0.18
                       left_mount_rpy:='1.247666407 -0.232161321 1.508064663'
                       right_mount_rpy:='-1.256457931 -0.033197491 1.699631975'">
    <material name="skin"><color rgba="0.85 0.72 0.60 1"/></material>
    <material name="shirt"><color rgba="0.25 0.35 0.55 1"/></material>
    <material name="pack"><color rgba="0.15 0.15 0.15 1"/></material>
    <material name="trouser"><color rgba="0.20 0.22 0.28 1"/></material>
    <material name="strap"><color rgba="0.10 0.10 0.12 1"/></material>
    <!-- Mount hardware reads as machined metal, distinct from the fabric
         of the pack, so the load path is legible at a glance. -->
    <material name="mount_metal"><color rgba="0.62 0.64 0.68 1"/></material>

    <!-- ===================== TORSO ===================== -->
    <!-- Link frame stays at world z=1.05. Chest is placed by the visual
         origin: centre z=1.22, spanning 0.98..1.46 (shoulder line). -->
    <link name="torso">
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.17" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.36 0.22 0.48"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.17" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.36 0.22 0.48"/></geometry>
        <material name="shirt"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="${parent}_to_torso" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${parent}"/><child link="torso"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 1.05" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- ===================== HEAD + NECK ===================== -->
    <!-- Link frame stays at world z=1.40. Head centre raised to 1.645 by
         the visual origin, putting the crown at exactly 1.75 m. -->
    <link name="head">
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.245" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><sphere radius="0.105"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.10" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.055" length="0.16"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.245" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><sphere radius="0.105"/></geometry>
        <material name="skin"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.10" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.055" length="0.16"/></geometry>
        <material name="skin"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="torso_to_head" type="fixed">
      <parent link="torso"/><child link="head"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0.35" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- ===================== PELVIS ===================== -->
    <link name="hips">
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.17" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.32 0.21 0.18"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.17" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.32 0.21 0.18"/></geometry>
        <material name="trouser"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="torso_to_hips" type="fixed">
      <parent link="torso"/><child link="hips"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 -0.28" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- ===================== LEGS =====================
         Thigh + shank + foot as three visuals on the existing leg link,
         so no new joints are needed. Hip centres widened to +/-0.09 via
         the visual x-offset; the link frames stay at +/-0.07. -->
    <link name="left_leg">
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="0.02 0 0.36" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.075" length="0.44"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0.02 0 0.36" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.075" length="0.44"/></geometry>
        <material name="trouser"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0.02 0 -0.08" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.055" length="0.44"/></geometry>
        <material name="trouser"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0.02 0.06 -0.29" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.10 0.26 0.06"/></geometry>
        <material name="pack"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="hips_to_left_leg" type="fixed">
      <parent link="hips"/><child link="left_leg"/>
      <origin xyz="0.07 0 -0.45" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <link name="right_leg">
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="-0.02 0 0.36" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.075" length="0.44"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="-0.02 0 0.36" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.075" length="0.44"/></geometry>
        <material name="trouser"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="-0.02 0 -0.08" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.055" length="0.44"/></geometry>
        <material name="trouser"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="-0.02 0.06 -0.29" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.10 0.26 0.06"/></geometry>
        <material name="pack"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="hips_to_right_leg" type="fixed">
      <parent link="hips"/><child link="right_leg"/>
      <origin xyz="-0.07 0 -0.45" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- ===================== HUMAN ARMS =====================
         The previous model had NONE - the render showed a torso with
         only the two Kinova arms, which is why the SRL arms read as the
         wearer's arms. Upper arm / forearm / hand, shoulder line
         z=1.43 matching the top of the chest box.

         THE POSTURE IS A VARIABLE, and the block below is GENERATED.
         Edit src/srl_teleop/srl_teleop/wearer_posture.py and run
         scripts/gen_wearer_posture_xacro.py; do not edit it here. The
         same table feeds mount_guard_node's geometric clearance model,
         and a posture that reaches one and not the other is a
         measurement that reports the old answer under a new name. -->
    <!-- BEGIN GENERATED WEARER ARMS - edit wearer_posture.py, not this -->
    <!-- Which posture the wearer holds. See wearer_posture.py;
         SRL_WEARER_ARMS to pick one. -->
    <xacro:property name="wearer_arms" value="$(optenv SRL_WEARER_ARMS down)"/>
    <!-- An unknown posture must STOP the build. A typo that silently
         falls back to the default is a sweep that measures the same
         wearer five times and reports it as five postures. -->
    <xacro:unless value="${wearer_arms == 'behind' or wearer_arms == 'down' or wearer_arms == 'folded' or wearer_arms == 'none' or wearer_arms == 'out'}">
      <!-- a property body is evaluated lazily and would never fire;
           an attribute is substituted eagerly, so this one does. -->
      <link name="unknown_wearer_arms_posture_${1/0}"/>
    </xacro:unless>
    <xacro:if value="${wearer_arms == 'behind'}">
      <!-- clasped behind the back, hands crossed at the small of the back -->
      <link name="human_left_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.196463 -0.063174 0.244627" rpy="0.434724 -3.04192 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.0604803 -0.139374 0.067571" rpy="0.100369 -1.89892 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.116158 -0.170464 -0.0436598" rpy="0.202086 -2.47965 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.196463 -0.063174 0.244627" rpy="0.434724 3.04192 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.0604803 -0.139374 0.067571" rpy="0.100369 1.89892 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="0.116158 -0.170464 -0.0436598" rpy="0.202086 2.47965 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:if>
    <xacro:if value="${wearer_arms == 'down'}">
      <!-- arms hanging at the sides (the shipped model) -->
      <link name="human_left_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.21 0 0.23" rpy="0 3.14159 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.21 0 -0.05" rpy="0 3.14159 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="0.21 0 -0.27" rpy="0 3.14159 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.21 0 0.23" rpy="0 -3.14159 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.21 0 -0.05" rpy="0 -3.14159 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.21 0 -0.27" rpy="0 -3.14159 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:if>
    <xacro:if value="${wearer_arms == 'folded'}">
      <!-- folded across the chest (the forearms are IN the work volume) -->
      <link name="human_left_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.217518 0.0270637 0.232653" rpy="-0.181418 3.09062 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.101566 0.0905183 0.103502" rpy="-0.283721 -1.42448 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.105478 0.140389 0.152252" rpy="-0.150341 -1.2203 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.217518 0.0270637 0.232653" rpy="-0.181418 -3.09062 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.101566 0.0905183 0.103502" rpy="-0.283721 1.42448 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="0.105478 0.140389 0.152252" rpy="-0.150341 1.2203 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:if>
    <xacro:if value="${wearer_arms == 'none'}">
      <!-- no wearer arms at all - the limit, not a posture -->
      <!-- no links: the wearer has no arms in this configuration -->
    </xacro:if>
    <xacro:if value="${wearer_arms == 'out'}">
      <!-- held out to the sides and back, elbows out, hands low and behind -->
      <link name="human_left_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.307141 -0.0523068 0.278375" rpy="0.356197 2.37875 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="0.497939 -0.169653 0.114313" rpy="0.523946 2.1588 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_left_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_left_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_left_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="0.654579 -0.28148 0.00778671" rpy="0.546699 2.18152 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_upper_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.05" length="0.3"/></geometry>
          <material name="shirt"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_upper_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_upper_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.307141 -0.0523068 0.278375" rpy="0.356197 -2.37875 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_lower_arm">
        <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="0.045" length="0.26"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_lower_arm" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_lower_arm"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.497939 -0.169653 0.114313" rpy="0.523946 -2.1588 0"/>
      </joint>
      <link name="human_right_hand">
        <collision><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry></collision>
        <visual><geometry><box size="0.09 0.05 0.18"/></geometry>
          <material name="skin"/></visual>
      </link>
      <joint name="torso_to_human_right_hand" type="fixed">
        <parent link="torso"/><child link="human_right_hand"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.654579 -0.28148 0.00778671" rpy="0.546699 -2.18152 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:if>
    <!-- END GENERATED WEARER ARMS -->

    <!-- ===================== HARNESS =====================
         Shoulder straps, so the pack reads as worn rather than stuck on. -->
    <link name="harness">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0.12 0.10 0.20" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.07 0.05 0.34"/></geometry>
        <material name="strap"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="-0.12 0.10 0.20" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.07 0.05 0.34"/></geometry>
        <material name="strap"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0.12 0.00 0.375" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.07 0.26 0.05"/></geometry>
        <material name="strap"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="-0.12 0.00 0.375" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.07 0.26 0.05"/></geometry>
        <material name="strap"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="torso_to_harness" type="fixed">
      <parent link="torso"/><child link="harness"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- ===================== BACKPACK =====================
         Frame unchanged at world (0, -0.12, 1.07). The body is placed by
         its visual origin so it sits against the enlarged torso. -->
    <link name="backpack">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 -0.095 0.155" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.44 0.25 0.45"/></geometry>
        <material name="pack"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="torso_to_backpack" type="fixed">
      <parent link="torso"/><child link="backpack"/>
      <origin xyz="0 -0.12 0.02" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- ===================== MOUNT STRUCTURE =====================
         A load-bearing plate spanning both mount points, proud of the
         pack so it reads as structure rather than fabric. Sized so the
         mount origins (x = +/-0.15, z = 0.18) fall INSIDE its volume -
         that, plus the pads below, is what stops the arms looking as
         though they float. -->
    <link name="mount_plate">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 -0.16 0.18" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.52 0.10 0.08"/></geometry>
        <material name="mount_metal"/>
      </visual>
      <!-- Vertical spine tying the plate down the pack, so the plate is
           not visually cantilevered off nothing. -->
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 -0.12 0.02" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.12 0.20 0.36"/></geometry>
        <material name="mount_metal"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="backpack_to_mount_plate" type="fixed">
      <parent link="backpack"/><child link="mount_plate"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- ===================== ARM MOUNTS =====================
         ORIGINS UNCHANGED. Exact mirrors about the sagittal plane, which
         in this frame convention is x=0, NOT y=0. Under a reflection
         through x=0 a rotation maps as (r, p, y) -> (r, -p, -y): roll is
         preserved, pitch and yaw negate. Verified numerically. -->
    <!-- rpy of Rx(-tilt)*Rz(clock) in URDF's ZYX convention, closed form.
         Both mounts are generated from the SAME expressions with clock
         negated for the right, so the pair is a mirror by construction and
         cannot be edited out of symmetry. -->
    <xacro:property name="mt" value="${radians(mount_tilt_deg)}"/>
    <xacro:property name="mc" value="${radians(mount_clock_deg)}"/>

    <link name="left_mount"/>
    <joint name="backpack_to_left_mount" type="fixed">
      <parent link="backpack"/><child link="left_mount"/>
      <origin xyz="${mount_x} ${mount_y} ${mount_z}" rpy="${left_mount_rpy}"/>
    </joint>

    <link name="right_mount"/>
    <joint name="backpack_to_right_mount" type="fixed">
      <parent link="backpack"/><child link="right_mount"/>
      <origin xyz="${-mount_x} ${mount_y} ${mount_z}" rpy="${right_mount_rpy}"/>
    </joint>

    <!-- Mounting bosses. Children of the mount links, so they inherit the
         mount tilt exactly and stay flush under the Kinova base no matter
         what the mount origin is later changed to. -->
    <link name="left_mount_pad">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 -0.02" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.065" length="0.04"/></geometry>
        <material name="mount_metal"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="left_mount_to_pad" type="fixed">
      <parent link="left_mount"/><child link="left_mount_pad"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <link name="right_mount_pad">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 -0.02" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="0.065" length="0.04"/></geometry>
        <material name="mount_metal"/>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <joint name="right_mount_to_pad" type="fixed">
      <parent link="right_mount"/><child link="right_mount_pad"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

  </xacro:macro>
</robot>
